        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}2x+3y&=12\\\\3x-4y&=-1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{45}{17},\\ y=\\frac{38}{17}$\n\nMultiply the equations by $4$ and $3$, then add to eliminate $y$.",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second by $3$, then add.\n$$\\begin{align*}8x+12y&=48\\\\9x-12y&=-3\\\\(8x+12y)+(9x-12y)&=48-3\\\\17x&=45\\\\x&=\\frac{45}{17}\\\\\\frac{90}{17}+3y&=12\\\\3y&=\\frac{114}{17}\\\\y&=\\frac{38}{17}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $\\frac{90+114}{17}=12$ and $\\frac{135-152}{17}=-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 69
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}5x-2y&=17\\\\4x+3y&=9\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3,\\ y=-1$",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second by $2$, then add.\n$$\\begin{align*}15x-6y&=51\\\\8x+6y&=18\\\\(15x-6y)+(8x+6y)&=51+18\\\\23x&=69\\\\x&=3\\\\15-2y&=17\\\\-2y&=2\\\\y&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $5(3)-2(-1)=17$ and $4(3)+3(-1)=9$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}2x+3y&=1\\\\5x+4y&=-1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1,\\ y=1$",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by $4$ and the second by $3$, then subtract the second result from the first.\n$$\\begin{align*}8x+12y&=4\\\\15x+12y&=-3\\\\(8x+12y)-(15x+12y)&=4-(-3)\\\\-7x&=7\\\\x&=-1\\\\-2+3y&=1\\\\3y&=3\\\\y&=1\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $2(-1)+3(1)=1$ and $5(-1)+4(1)=-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}3x-5y&=-21\\\\5x+3y&=-19\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{79}{17},\\ y=\\frac{24}{17}$\n\nMultiply the equations by $3$ and $5$, then add to eliminate $y$.",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second by $5$, then add.\n$$\\begin{align*}9x-15y&=-63\\\\25x+15y&=-95\\\\(9x-15y)+(25x+15y)&=-63-95\\\\34x&=-158\\\\x&=-\\frac{79}{17}\\\\-\\frac{237}{17}-5y&=-21\\\\-5y&=-\\frac{120}{17}\\\\y&=\\frac{24}{17}\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $\\frac{-237-120}{17}=-21$ and $\\frac{-395+72}{17}=-19$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 69
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}4x-y&=-3\\\\5x+3y&=-8\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1,\\ y=-1$",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by $3$, then add the second.\n$$\\begin{align*}12x-3y&=-9\\\\(12x-3y)+(5x+3y)&=-9-8\\\\17x&=-17\\\\x&=-1\\\\-4-y&=-3\\\\y&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $4(-1)-(-1)=-3$ and $5(-1)+3(-1)=-8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q5-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}6x-5y&=8\\\\3x+2y&=13\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3,\\ y=2$",
          "worked": "Multiply the second equation by $2$, then subtract the first.\n$$\\begin{align*}6x+4y&=26\\\\(6x+4y)-(6x-5y)&=26-8\\\\9y&=18\\\\y&=2\\\\3x+4&=13\\\\3x&=9\\\\x&=3\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $6(3)-5(2)=8$ and $3(3)+2(2)=13$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q5-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}4a+3b&=22\\\\2a-5b&=-2\\end{aligned}$$",
