        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=5,\\ b=3$",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by $3$ and the second by $4$, then subtract the first result from the second.\n$$\\begin{align*}9a-12b&=9\\\\28a-12b&=104\\\\(28a-12b)-(9a-12b)&=104-9\\\\19a&=95\\\\a&=5\\\\15-4b&=3\\\\-4b&=-12\\\\b&=3\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $3(5)-4(3)=3$ and $7(5)-3(3)=26$.",
